flowchart LR
    accTitle: Airflow task execution, storage and worker autoscaling
    accDescr: DAG files are baked into all Airflow images. The DAG processor serializes definitions, schedulers submit Celery workloads to Redis, workers use the internal execution API, and KEDA queries task state in PostgreSQL to scale workers.

    subgraph compute["Airflow namespace"]
        direction TB
        files["Bundled DAGs + cluster policy<br/>/opt/airflow/dags<br/>/opt/airflow/config"]
        parser["DAG processor x1<br/>Parse / ownership / DAG grants"]
        scheduler["Schedulers x2<br/>Schedule runs and submit workloads"]
        worker["Celery worker Deployment<br/>1 to 3 replicas / 2 processes each<br/>Department pools: 2 slots each"]
        api["API servers x2<br/>UI / REST / internal Execution API"]
        trigger["Triggerer x1<br/>Deferrable task triggers"]
        files -->|Parse| parser
        files -->|Load task code| worker
        worker -->|HTTP :8080 /execution/ + task JWT| api
    end

    subgraph state["Docker data services"]
        metadata[("PostgreSQL: airflow<br/>DAGs / runs / task state<br/>Celery result backend")]
        warehouse[("PostgreSQL: warehouse<br/>Seeded demo_transactions<br/>Read-only warehouse role")]
        broker[("Redis broker<br/>Password authentication / AOF")]
        storage[("MinIO<br/>Run-specific finance reports<br/>Remote task logs")]
        secrets["Vault<br/>aws_default / smtp_default<br/>warehouse_default"]
    end

    trigger -->|Deferred trigger state and events| metadata
    parser -->|Serialized DAG definitions and permissions| metadata
    scheduler <-->|Scheduling and run state| metadata
    scheduler -->|Submit Celery workload| broker
    worker -->|Consume workload| broker
    worker -->|Celery result backend| metadata
    api <-->|Metadata transactions| metadata
    worker -->|Analytics SELECT| warehouse
    worker -->|Upload task logs and report| storage
    api -->|Read remote task logs| storage
    worker -->|TLS + ServiceAccount login| secrets

    subgraph scaling["AUTOSCALING"]
        keda["KEDA PostgreSQL scaler<br/>Poll every 15 seconds<br/>Count queued + running tasks / 2"]
        hpa["Kubernetes HPA<br/>Worker minimum 1 / maximum 3"]
        keda -->|External metric| hpa
    end
    keda -->|Read task_instance state| metadata
    hpa -.->|Desired worker replicas| worker

    classDef compute fill:#eaf2ff,stroke:#6389be,color:#172b4d
    classDef data fill:#e5f7f0,stroke:#46977c,color:#153f32
    classDef identity fill:#fff4d6,stroke:#c59b38,color:#594214
    classDef control fill:#f0eaff,stroke:#9673c8,color:#3e285c
    class files,parser,scheduler,worker,api,trigger compute
    class metadata,warehouse,broker,storage data
    class secrets identity
    class keda,hpa control
